          "worked": "From part a, $y=\\sqrt{1-x^2}$ with $-1\\le x\\le1$ and $y\\ge0$.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}y^2&=1-x^2\\\\x^2+y^2&=1.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nDraw the upper half of the unit circle, including both endpoints.",
